cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data, code, or these materials, please cite the paper."
title: "reranker-failure-transitions: data, code, and materials for semantic failure-state transitions across heterogeneous rerankers"
abstract: >-
  Data, code, and materials for analyzing semantic failure-state transitions, passage identity, and projection effects across heterogeneous rerankers.
  Six rerankers of differing paradigms are run over an identical frozen
  10-candidate pool for 3,719 QASPER queries across two retrieval arms; each
  rank-1 passage is adjudicated into one of five semantic states, and pairwise
  state transitions are classified as Resolved, Persistent, Transformed, or
  Regressed. Includes the frozen candidate pools, reranker outputs, adjudication labels,
  prompts, model locks, and a single script that reproduces every table.
